{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794857719925487913,"compiled_state":{"alias":"citreous-talented-wildebeest","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"d4386434f0627df9bf35ccf973acfbc0f1aed64ab0242cbd7a8580b3272e7c0e","event_uuid":"12570962-f34c-4abb-911c-935080f2bf10","position":{"commit_sha":"0b21f116c1802c34a71a103f264393bde4d6a736","position":"1794857604949608792-12570962-f34c-4abb-911c-935080f2bf10"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"181b63af2f2ce324ddff0abbd1de3be16086649dd9d1d867ae243b84371a5718","event_uuid":"557de8ce-8bf8-4879-a9b1-fa90bbed9b34","position":{"commit_sha":"d97885316e785e1c97e3b37152ddc7c3cea2c4e5","position":"1794857719925487912-557de8ce-8bf8-4879-a9b1-fa90bbed9b34"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794857604949608792,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"557de8ce-8bf8-4879-a9b1-fa90bbed9b34","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6798-606d-37dc-46e7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job runs a maintained subset held green: tests known to fail on Windows are deselected through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-shell.args`. This bug owns that file: 143 tests in 23 modules, from the 5 scheduled runs at `b4e0d01b649` (2026-11-15/16).\n\nTests run `bash`, `/bin/sh` or `.sh` scripts. On the runner `bash` resolves to the WSL launcher with no distribution installed, which prints UTF-16 `Windows Subsystem for Linux has no installed distributions` and exits 1; `/bin/sh` is drive-relative and not found.\n\nLargest modules: `tests/unit/test_gate_step_tree_skew.py` (81, runs workflow step bodies under `bash`), `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py` (10), `tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py` (7), `tests/scripts/test_feature_branch_e2e_scenario4.py` (6), `tests/unit/test_session_shims.py` (6).\n\nExample: `tests/scripts/test_feature_branch_inventory.py::test_rebased_content_equivalent_branch_reports_merged`: `AssertionError: returncode=1`.\n\n## Approach\n\nPer module decide: make the test portable (Python instead of shell), or skip on the missing capability (keyed on the capability, as bug subatomic-unwashed-macaw did with `os.access('/bin/sh', os.X_OK)`), never on `os.name`.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe failing product or test code for this class, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-shell.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Testing\n\nPOSIX: the touched tests still pass under `make verify`. Windows: a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the change (scheduled, or `gh workflow run test.yml --ref main`) passes with the removed lines no longer deselected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `posix-shell.args` names a test that passed (or skipped with a capability reason) in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"b93b-40ce-0da3-4c67","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: tests assume a POSIX shell (143 tests)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["12570962-f34c-4abb-911c-935080f2bf10","557de8ce-8bf8-4879-a9b1-fa90bbed9b34"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794857719925487913,"uuid":"8291d2b2-98a4-40a3-8e3e-c751693e30ef"}